# Version control exists here for ONE reason: on 2026-08-03 an agent's edit sliced
# world/items/HUMAN-REFERENCE.md from a heading to end of file, 1,655 lines -> 538.
# There was no git, no backup, and the content was not recoverable from the
# transcript. Sections 000 and 1-7 -- the layer map, the LOD table, and the
# amplitude/frequency traps and guard rails, i.e. the "how to build a figure"
# half -- are PERMANENTLY LOST.
#
# So: track the SOURCE and the REASONING. Do not track the artefacts, which are
# large, regenerable, and would make commits useless.

# Renders, blends, caches, bakes -- all regenerable, all enormous
*.blend
*.blend1
*.blend2
*.png
*.jpg
*.exr
*.npz
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp4
*.bphys
render/
work/
sim/tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Large generated data. The DOCS in docs/ are tracked; these are not.
docs/screen_presence*.json
docs/screen_presence*_objects.json
docs/*_points.npz
docs/beat_sheet.json
docs/collision_report.json
docs/placement*.json
docs/depth_probe.json
docs/instance_variety.json
docs/presentation_normals.json
docs/inventory_iter.json

# Telemetry is generated from the spec, but it IS the single source of truth for
# motion AND audio and it has been wrong in ways that took a day to find. Track it.
!telemetry/telemetry.csv
